<% page title: "Privacy policy",
        description: "What Trellis collects, why, who helps us run it, and how you stay in control of your data." %>

<article class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pb-12 pt-12 sm:px-6 sm:pt-16">
  <div class="prose-warm">
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl text-ink sm:text-5xl">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">Last updated <%= Site::POLICIES_UPDATED %></p>

    <div class="card space-y-2 bg-peach-50/70">
      <p class="font-bold">The short version</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Organizations put information into Trellis to run their work. <strong>That information belongs to them</strong>, and we use it only to run Trellis for them.</li>
        <li>We don't sell personal information, we don't show ads, and we never market to the people in your network.</li>
        <li>This website sets no cookies and has no trackers.</li>
        <li>You can export your data, and ask us to correct or delete it.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      Trellis is run by <%= Site::COMPANY %> ("<strong>we</strong>", "<strong>us</strong>"). This policy
      covers the Trellis application at app.visittrellis.com and this website. It works alongside our
      <a href="<%= path("terms/") %>">terms of service</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Two kinds of information</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Information organizations put into Trellis.</strong> A network (an organization's space in
      Trellis) stores information about its members, volunteers, partners and the people it serves: names,
      contact details, applications, survey answers, records of its work, and files. The network decides what
      to collect and who in the network can see it; we hold and process it on the network's behalf and follow
      its instructions. If you're a member of a network and have a question about your information there, the
      network's organizers are usually the best people to ask first. We'll help them, or you, either way.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Information we need to run the Service.</strong> Your account details, how you sign in, and the
      technical information that keeps Trellis secure and working. For this information, we decide how it's
      used, as described below.
    </p>

    <h2>3. What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Account details:</strong> your email address, name, and password. Passwords are stored only as a one-way hash; we can't read them.</li>
      <li><strong>Google sign-in,</strong> if you choose it: your name, email address and Google account identifier. We don't get access to your Google data beyond that.</li>
      <li><strong>Your network's data:</strong> whatever you and your network put in, as above. Some sensitive details, like phone numbers, are encrypted in our database.</li>
      <li><strong>History:</strong> a record of changes to your network's data, so organizers can see who changed what and when.</li>
      <li><strong>Usage and technical information:</strong> when you use the app we record visits and actions within it, along with your IP address, browser and device type, to keep it secure, fix problems and understand which parts of Trellis people use. This is kept in our own database, not shared with analytics or advertising companies.</li>
      <li><strong>Email:</strong> messages Trellis sends for you or your network (sign-in links, password resets, announcements, campaigns) and whether they were delivered.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>This website</strong> (visittrellis.com) sets no cookies, loads nothing from third parties, and
      runs no analytics. <strong>The app</strong> (app.visittrellis.com) uses cookies only to keep you signed
      in, remember your current network, and protect forms from forgery.
    </p>

    <h2>5. How we use information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To provide Trellis: sign you in, show you and your network the right things, and send the email the Service needs to send.</li>
      <li>To keep Trellis and its users safe: preventing abuse, investigating problems, and keeping backups.</li>
      <li>To support you when you ask for help.</li>
      <li>To improve Trellis, mostly by understanding which features are used. We don't use your network's data to build products for anyone else.</li>
      <li>To meet legal obligations.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We don't sell personal information, share it for advertising, or use it to profile anyone.</p>

    <h2>6. Who helps us run Trellis</h2>
    <p>We use a small number of service providers, who process information only to provide their service to us:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Heroku</strong> (Salesforce): hosting the app and its database.</li>
      <li><strong>Amazon Web Services:</strong> storing files and images uploaded to Trellis.</li>
      <li><strong>Mailer To Go:</strong> sending email.</li>
      <li><strong>Google:</strong> sign-in, only if you choose "Sign in with Google".</li>
      <li><strong>GitHub Pages:</strong> hosting this website. Like any web host, it sees visitors' IP addresses.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We may also share information if the law requires it, to protect people's safety, or as part of a sale or
      merger of our business, in which case this policy would continue to apply to it.
    </p>

    <h2>7. How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      We keep your network's data for as long as the network exists. When a network is closed, its owners have
      at least 30 days to export the data, and then we delete it, including from backups as they cycle out.
      Account details are kept while your account is open. Technical logs are kept only as long as they're
      useful for security and troubleshooting.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Your choices and rights</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>See and change it:</strong> you can update your own profile in Trellis at any time.</li>
      <li><strong>Take it with you:</strong> network owners can export their data or download a full backup from inside Trellis.</li>
      <li><strong>Delete it:</strong> you can ask us to delete your account. Information a network holds about you is the network's to manage, and we'll work with them on your request.</li>
      <li><strong>Ask us:</strong> depending on where you live, you may have further rights to access, correct, delete, or object to how your information is used. Write to us and we'll respond within 30 days.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>9. Security</h2>
    <p>
      All traffic to Trellis is encrypted. Each network's data is kept separate from every other network's,
      sensitive fields are encrypted at rest, and access is limited by each person's role. No system is
      perfectly secure; if a breach ever affects your information, we'll tell you promptly.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Children</h2>
    <p>
      Trellis accounts are for people 13 and older. Networks that work with younger people are responsible for
      getting the consent the law requires before entering information about them.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If we change this policy in a way that matters, we'll tell network owners before it takes effect. The date
      at the top shows when it last changed.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Privacy questions or requests: <a href="mailto:<%= Site::CONTACT_EMAIL %>"><%= Site::CONTACT_EMAIL %></a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</article>
